From 50aaca643038774b6779c911c4f96bc7e0d607e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bui duc phuc <phucduc.bui@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 17:38:16 +0700
Subject: ASoC: atmel: atmel-pcm-pdc: Fix atmel_pcm_close() being skipped on rollback
Git-commit: 50aaca643038774b6779c911c4f96bc7e0d607e9
Patch-mainline: v7.4-rc1
References: git-fixes

snd_pcm_hw_constraint_integer() may return 1, which is then returned
from atmel_pcm_open(). ASoC only marks the component as opened
when .open() returns 0, so .close() can be skipped on rollback.

Return 0 explicitly on success.

Fixes: 92dfa6198623 ("ASoC: atmel-pcm: split into two file")
Signed-off-by: bui duc phuc <phucduc.bui@gmail.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20261008103831.542533-10-phucduc.bui@gmail.com
Signed-off-by: Mark Brown <broonie@kernel.org>
Acked-by: Takashi Iwai <tiwai@suse.de>

---
 sound/soc/atmel/atmel-pcm-pdc.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/atmel/atmel-pcm-pdc.c b/sound/soc/atmel/atmel-pcm-pdc.c
index 374f93fa6e0b..552bfa30d4ba 100644
--- a/sound/soc/atmel/atmel-pcm-pdc.c
+++ b/sound/soc/atmel/atmel-pcm-pdc.c
@@ -295,6 +295,8 @@ static int atmel_pcm_open(struct snd_soc_component *component,
 	}
 	runtime->private_data = prtd;
 
+	return 0;
+
  out:
 	return ret;
 }
